  "sections": [
    {
      "selector": "#what",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1504,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1177,
      "heading": "You paste a link and it does the walking.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "01 How it works You paste a link and it does the walking. Walkcast opens your website in a real browser, signs in, clicks through your pages and records the whole visit as a video file you can share. THE OLD WAY Write the script, record the screen, retake it, record the voice, sync the captions. Then you ship one update, and it is already out of date. 01 Paste a link Give it the address of a site you own or may test, and the sign-in details if the site needs one. 02 It signs in and walks the site A real Chromium browser opens the page, signs in like a first-time user, and visits up to 30 pages",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2681,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 817,
      "heading": "Fast enough to re-run on every release. Strict enough to point at production.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "BY THE NUMBERS Fast enough to re-run on every release. Strict enough to point at production. <1 min to record and encode a six-page site on an ordinary laptop 30 pages walked in one recording, on one site, paced and polite 0 passwords written to disk. Held in memory for the run, then dropped $0 per seat for every feature, on every machine, with no trial clock Password never on disk Stops at CAPTCHA and 2FA Never submits a form No analytics in the app Recordings stay on your PC",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#compare",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3498,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1497,
      "heading": "Loom films you. Walkcast films your site.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Loom",
        "Screen Studio",
        "Scribe",
        "vs Loom",
        "vs Screen Studio",
        "vs Scribe"
      ],
      "text": "02 Compared Loom films you. Walkcast films your site. Screen recorders need someone at the keyboard, a microphone and an edit. Walkcast drives its own browser, so the tour comes out the same every time you re-run it. Here is the honest version, including where the others are better. Walkcast compared with Loom, Screen Studio and Scribe Walkcast Loom Screen Studio Scribe Price for one person $0 MIT, forever $18 per month $29 a month, or $108 a year $23 per month WHERE WALKCAST IS BUILT FOR THE JOB The whole visit recorded with nobody on camera Yes No No No Signs in and walks the site on its own",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#login",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4994,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1476,
      "heading": "Records the pages only users see. Your password never hits disk.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "03 Behind the login Records the pages only users see. Your password never hits disk. Walkcast finds the sign-in form, including two-step email-then-password flows, signs in with what you give it, and walks the signed-in site. Held in memory only Stops at CAPTCHA and 2FA Read-only after sign-in Same site, respects robots.txt Walkcast · Record Ready Site link app.est Username Password I own this site or may test it Record estate360.in Run log 0 steps password [hidden] You confirm the site Every recording asks you to say you own the site or may test it. Leave it unticked and there is no recording",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#studio",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 6471,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 2137,
      "heading": "One run, five files. Every page visited, with its status.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "04 The app One run, five files. Every page visited, with its status. Walks the whole site in one go. Visits your site the way a first-time user would, page by page, and records all of it. / /product /pricing /contact /login /signup /dashboard /leads 30 pages per recording 8 by default, 30 at most. Same site only. Paced, and robots.txt is respected. Every format. Same take. .mp4 .webm 5 files per run MP4, WebM, captions, a transcript and the page list. REC HD The whole visit H.264 video with captions on, ready to share. Works with your setup. Install on Windows, sign in to the site you test, an",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#uses",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8607,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 672,
      "heading": "One recorder. Six ways to use the same visit.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Pause animations"
      ],
      "text": "One recorder. Six ways to use the same visit. Pause animations Step 1 of 4 Onboarding Show new users around before their first login. Opening the product page. Product demos A full product tour for sales calls, from one link. captions.vtt Help articles Drop the video and its transcript into a support doc. /pricing 200 /product 200 /billing 500 QA evidence A recorded pass over the site, with every status. Client handover Walk the client through the site you built, no call. v2.4 → v2.5 Release notes Record what changed after every deploy. Step 1 of 4 Onboarding Show new users around before their",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#pricing",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 9279,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 720,
      "heading": "Free to use. For the whole team.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Download free",
        "Pricing details"
      ],
      "text": "05 Pricing Free to use. For the whole team. Every feature is in the free download. Walkcast is MIT licensed and runs on your own machine, so there is no server bill to pass on to you and nothing to sign up for. Unlimited recordings and seats Up to 30 pages per recording MP4, WebM, captions, transcript Voice-over with your own key, or offline Download free Pricing details What a team of 5 people pays in a year 1 25 50 Loom $1,080 Business, $18 per user a month Screen Studio $540 Yearly, $108 per person Scribe $708 Team, $59 a month for 5, then $12 each Walkcast $0 Every feature, every seat Pric",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#agents",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 9999,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1108,
      "heading": "Building a browser AI agent? The Lab shows why it failed.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Download free",
        "Read the Lab docs"
      ],
      "text": "06 Also in the app: Walkcast Lab Building a browser AI agent? The Lab shows why it failed. Most people only need the video recorder above. If you build AI agents that use a browser, the same app has a Lab. When an agent fails a task, it shows the cause and the evidence, and turns the failure into a test you can rerun on the next version. It is in the sidebar under Lab. THE RECORDER · FOR EVERYONE A video tour of your site, without a script Founders, marketers and PMs paste one link and get the whole visit as an MP4 with captions, a transcript and a voice-over. Pages behind a login are included",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#faq",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 11107,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1278,
      "heading": "Before you press record.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Ask on GitHub",
        "01What is Walkcast?",
        "02Is Walkcast a screen recorder?",
        "03What is Walkcast Lab?",
        "04Which computers does Walkcast run on?",
        "05How do I make a narrated video walkthrough of my website?",
        "06Can it record pages behind a login?",
        "07Is my password stored?"
      ],
      "text": "Before you press record. Everything you might want to know before your first recording. Still have a question? Open an issue and we will help you get set up. Ask on GitHub 01 What is Walkcast? Walkcast is a free, open-source desktop app (Windows and Linux) that makes a video tour of your website from one link. A real browser signs in, visits up to 30 pages the way a first-time user would (8 by default) and returns the complete recording as an MP4 with WebVTT captions and a transcript. A voice-over is included when you add a voice key. Every caption comes from what the browser actually did. 02 ",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#get",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12385,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1067,
      "heading": "Your site has pages. Now it has a video tour.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF8F3",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Download for Windows",
        "download page",
        "Kunj Shah",
        "open an issue"
      ],
      "text": "Your site has pages. Now it has a video tour. REC 00:00:00 walkthrough.mp4 1:11 · H.264 captions.vtt 13 lines transcript.txt 6 pages narration.wav optional voice Your tour is one click away. Download for Windows Free. Windows and Linux. Version 0.8.1. The installers are not code-signed yet, so Windows may show \"Windows protected your PC\". That is expected, and the download page has the steps to get past it. Built by Kunj Shah. If it does not do what you need, open an issue and tell us what you were trying to do.",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
